                <pb facs="0475" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg407"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. de Stoeckl to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Imperial Legation of Russia to the
                                United States</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 23, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary:</hi> Captain Pestchourooff,
                    commissioner of the imperial government for the transfer of our former
                    possessions in America, informs me that the Russian ship Czaritsa is expected at
                    Sitka with provisions and goods for the Russian American Company.</p>
                <p>As this vessel left Europe at the beginning of the year, before the conclusion of
                    the treaty of cession, it is but just that the cargo of the Czaritsa be admitted
                    free of duty in case it reaches its place of destination after the establishment
                    of the United States custom-house system at Sitka.</p>
                <p>I take the liberty, Mr. Secretary of State, to recommend this affair particularly
                    to the benevolent courtesy which the federal government has always exercised in
                    its transactions with the imperial government.</p>
                <p>Please accept, Mr. Secretary of State, the assurance of my very high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>STOECKL.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
